@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] buck2-wrapper-pinned-cells
tools/buck2 MUST exec only the buck2 from the flake-pinned buckCells and MUST
rebuild .buck-cells whenever an input of buckCells may have changed, killing
the daemon only when the cells store path actually changed (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] precommit-wrapper-file-sets
tools/precommit MUST pass buck/bxl/precommit.bxl every changed path of its
scope (the named or staged files plus staged deletions; merge-base..working
tree for --base; every check for --all), MUST unset GIT_* before starting
Buck2, MUST rewrite files only under --fix, and MUST fail with the checks'
findings. When Buck2 cannot start it MUST run the pre-M8 hook scripts
directly over the same files, naming the checks it skipped, rather than pass
silently (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] precommit-unconfigured-graph
tools/precommit MUST fail before its checks when `uquery 'deps(//...)'` does
not resolve. Unconfigured traversal follows every select branch, as the target
hashes of tools/affected do, so a dependency that only an unselected branch
names (toolchains//:cxx_no_default_deps) is caught locally rather than by CI
target selection (ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] machine-test-failure-log
tools/machine-test-log MUST write the complete Nix build log of a
nixos_machine_test target's derivation, named by its `.assembly[drv]`
evaluation, so CI can print and upload the subtest and VM console output of
a failed machine test after the runner is gone (ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] buck2-no-nix-mode
tools/buck2 --no-nix MUST exec only a buck2 whose release asset and prelude
archive match tools/buck2-no-nix.json and the pin registry's SHA-256 (or the
OVERALLS_BUCK2_KIT copy of a //tools:buck2-no-nix-<os> kit built from the
same pins), materialised in .buck-cells as a real directory. Its configuration
enables only non_hermetic targets, so a runner without Nix never builds a
hermetic target from PATH tools (ADR-0269 M9).
